WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:01.899
(audience cheering)

00:00:01.899 --> 00:00:03.830
- Oh, thank you, thank you all.

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:05.800
And, oh, thank you, man, for...

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.370
God, did it again!

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.850
Awesome!

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.290
Well, as Denzel says,

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:16.110
we've come a long way
and done a lot of things,

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:20.533
so I'm really, really proud
to receive this statue.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.570
Another standout memory to
add to our shared experiences.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:27.850
This is awesome.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:32.223
First, thank you, governors,
for this incredible honor.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:34.580
Who knew, you know, a little kid

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.840
from Chattanooga, Tennessee,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.200
watching movies and
wishing he could be here,

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.590
would get the votes of people

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.247
who run an organization
like this that says,

00:00:43.247 --> 00:00:45.160
"Hey, I deserve something like this"?

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.227
Thank you so very much.

00:00:46.227 --> 00:00:49.227
(audience clapping)

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.600
And I will say when I
got this call last year,

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.800
it was totally unexpected,

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.710
but I guarantee you this
thing's gonna be cherished.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:01.300
As long as I dreamt, and imagined,

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.650
and practiced this speech,

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:03.870
you know, oughta be a piece of cake.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.533
But (sighs) it's not.

00:01:09.097 --> 00:01:11.520
"Together for Days," Stan,

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.133
my first film credit in 1972
to here, 50 years later.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:20.350
It's been a real pleasure
making indelible impressions

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:23.783
on audiences as Gang Member Number Two,

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.940
Bum, Hold Up Man,

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:30.426
and the unforgettable, Black Guy.

00:01:30.426 --> 00:01:32.250
(audience laughing)

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.363
Just to name a few.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.900
But every little taste of
this biz made me want more.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.620
All those Saturdays I spent
at the Liberty and the Grand,

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.560
the segregated theaters
of my youth and childhood

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:46.580
in Chattanooga, Tennessee,

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:50.220
imagining that I was Errol
Flynn or Kirk Douglas,

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:54.350
or even James Cagney, even John Wayne.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:57.750
But going home and
recreating those stories

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.533
with my friends or just by myself.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.090
Being awed during the Blaxploitation era,

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:07.547
wishing I was up on that
screen and wondering,

00:02:07.547 --> 00:02:10.190
"How the hell do you get
in a movie like that?"

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:11.920
Discovering Peter Sellers, Bond,

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.250
the Shaw Brothers, George Lucas.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:17.630
I knew I loved it, I just didn't
know how to make it happen.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:22.593
And, fortunately, when it
did, in 1990, I was sober.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:27.300
Loved and supported by
my wife and daughter.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.730
My reasons for being,

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.380
and my biggest critics,

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.667
and my biggest fans.

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:34.667
(audience clapping)

00:02:38.487 --> 00:02:42.640
I knew very little about
navigating this world,

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.230
but I was gifted with
a wonderful publicist

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:47.303
named Lisa Kasteler.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:52.160
Who had to explain to me what she did,

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.810
and then she went out and did it.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.193
Then came Eli Selden.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.980
She came to a location shoot,

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.410
contract in hand for a
movie and a proposition

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:04.160
I couldn't refuse to be my manager.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:05.957
Thank you, E.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:11.840
She, in turn, led me to
ICM and Carla Hacken,

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:16.559
who paired me with the
legend that is Toni Howard.

00:03:16.559 --> 00:03:19.120
(audience clapping)

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.713
And Carter Cohn.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:25.280
And the piece de resistance showed up,

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.913
my lawyer, Deborah Klein.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.970
Too amazing to describe

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.690
are the engines of what became

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.420
and continues to be a
rather decent career,

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:40.287
with the extra added piece
of Karen (indistinct).

00:03:41.329 --> 00:03:42.590
(audience clapping)

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.320
A gigantic thanks to
each and every one of you

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:48.040
for the scripts, the
deals, the faith in me,

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.250
the push to be better,

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.270
and making sure I lived
in the comfort zone

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:54.120
of knowing what the
next two jobs would be.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.353
'Cause, you know I love you for that.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:00.490
John Rigney and Level
Four, a wink and a nod,

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:01.807
and a thanks for that call

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:04.560
I asked you to make to
me when you made it.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.760
The dream has been shared
with my partner in crime,

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.760
my critic in residence,

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:11.653
my rock-solid foundation,

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.428
and my best friend, LaTanya.

00:04:15.428 --> 00:04:18.428
(audience clapping)

00:04:20.030 --> 00:04:24.410
We wanted to be Burton and Taylor,

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.690
but the Richardson-Jackson-Jackson pairing

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.163
has been quite formidable.

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:33.770
You've allowed me to indulge
my work habit to excess,

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:36.463
a lot of times, at the
expense of your own ambition.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.570
This award is a shared accomplishment.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:43.170
It's always been a two-man show.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:46.940
A laugh out loud, thanks to Zoe,

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.850
for going to work with
me all over the world

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:52.480
and indulging my movie taste
as a viewer and a daughter.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.580
And when I got the opportunity,

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:57.443
I tried to represent this
business the best I knew how.

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.150
I got out there to entertain audiences

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:03.970
the way Hollywood entertained me.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.910
Make them forget their
lives for a few hours

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:09.230
and be thrilled, awed, or
excited in the big room

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.630
where make believe lives.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:13.610
Thanks to every person
that's ever bought a ticket

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.003
to any movie I was in.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:20.320
It's truly been an honor and
a pleasure to entertain you.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.510
QT, thanks for the characters.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.850
Little Rob, I know you back there!

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:29.360
Robert Louis Stevenson, the
man who created all those wigs.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.007
Every time I asked him, I said to him,

00:05:31.007 --> 00:05:33.223
"Make me somebody," and he did.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:38.573
Once again, thank you,
governors, for the recognition.

00:05:39.441 --> 00:05:44.441
It's an honor.
(audience cheering)

